# MealPlanner API. Run with the Visual Studio / VS Code HTTP client.
# Set your own values in an http-client.env.json or edit the variables below locally (do not commit passwords).
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5169
@email = marc@example.com
@password = change-me
@apiKey = mp_paste-a-key-here

### Log in (sets the auth cookie for the following requests)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

### Who am I
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me

### Create an API key for the Claude connector. The key is shown only in this response.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/api-keys
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Claude (privat konto)" }

### List my API keys
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/api-keys

### Revoke a key
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/api-keys/1

### Search offers (cookie or API key). period: today | week | upcoming
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/offers?text=kyllingebryst&period=week
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Offers without an ingredient
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/offers?unmapped=true&limit=20

### Map an offer to an ingredient (creates the ingredient when a category is given)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/offers/1/mapping
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ingredients": ["Smør"], "category": "Mejeri" }

### MCP: list tools (API key only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/mcp
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{ "jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "method": "tools/list" }
